1
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:09,560
On a hiking map, the scale is 1 to 25,000.

2
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:16,230
The path from the car park to a waterfall measures 12 centimetres on the map.

3
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:18,930
How far is the real walk, in kilometres?

4
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:22,490
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:29,190
Every 1 centimetre on the map is 25,000 centimetres on the ground.

6
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:33,710
12 times 25,000 is 300,000 centimetres.

7
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,650
Divide by 100 to get metres: 3,000 metres.

8
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:42,710
Divide by 1,000 to get kilometres: 3 kilometres.

9
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:49,890
Remember: 100 centimetres make 1 metre, and 1,000 metres make 1 kilometre.

10
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:54,330
So 100,000 centimetres make 1 kilometre.

11
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:59,140
A scale tells you how distances on a map compare with real distances.

12
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:01,930
You can write a scale in 2 ways.

13
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:06,240
In words: 1 centimetre represents 2 kilometres.

14
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:08,670
Or as a ratio: 1 to 200,000.

15
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,500
A ratio has no units.

16
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:17,570
It means 1 of any unit on the map is 200,000 of the same unit in real life.

17
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:18,330
Your turn.

18
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:21,170
1 centimetre represents 4 kilometres.

19
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,780
What does 9 centimetres represent?

20
00:01:23,830 --> 00:01:27,250
Pause the video and try it.

21
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,030
Each centimetre is 4 kilometres.

22
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,920
9 times 4 is 36 kilometres.

23
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:37,030
Architects draw plans of rooms and buildings to scale.

24
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,010
A common scale is 1 to 50.

25
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:43,820
1 centimetre on the plan is 50 centimetres in real life.

26
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:48,280
A room is 8 centimetres by 6 centimetres on the plan.

27
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:53,080
Multiply by 50: it is 400 centimetres by 300 centimetres.

28
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:56,070
That is 4 metres by 3 metres.

29
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:56,810
Your turn.

30
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:59,110
A plan has a scale of 1 to 100.

31
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,310
A wall is 3.6 centimetres long on the plan.

32
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:05,060
How long is the real wall, in metres?

33
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:08,460
Pause the video and try it.

34
00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:11,920
3.6 times 100 is 360 centimetres.

35
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:14,460
That is 3.6 metres.

36
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:15,830
Here is the method.

37
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:19,100
Step 1: measure accurately on the map.

38
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:23,020
Step 2: from the map to real life, multiply by the scale.

39
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:25,900
From real life to the map, divide.

40
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:31,420
Step 3: with a ratio scale, the answer is in the same units as you started with.

41
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:33,070
Then convert it.

42
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,790
Step 4: check that your answer is sensible.

43
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,840
The scale is 1 to 40,000.

44
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:42,120
A road is 9 centimetres long on the map.

45
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:44,800
How long is the real road?

46
00:02:44,850 --> 00:02:49,720
9 times 40,000 is 360,000 centimetres.

47
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:54,500
Divide by 100,000 to change centimetres to kilometres.

48
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:57,880
The road is 3.6 kilometres long.

49
00:02:57,930 --> 00:03:00,150
A lake is 800 metres long.

50
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:05,230
How long is it on a map with a scale of 1 to 20,000?

51
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:07,960
First change to centimetres.

52
00:03:08,010 --> 00:03:11,730
800 metres is 80,000 centimetres.

53
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:14,740
From real life to the map, divide.

54
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:17,380
80,000 divided by 20,000 is 4.

55
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:21,640
The lake is 4 centimetres long on the map.

56
00:03:21,690 --> 00:03:23,650
A road is 3 kilometres long.

57
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:26,160
It measures 6 centimetres on a map.

58
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:28,640
Write the scale as a ratio.

59
00:03:28,690 --> 00:03:30,560
Use the same units.

60
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:34,200
3 kilometres is 300,000 centimetres.

61
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:37,670
So the ratio is 6 to 300,000.

62
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:39,860
Divide both parts by 6.

63
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:42,790
The scale is 1 to 50,000.

64
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:44,720
The scale is 1 to 30,000.

65
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:47,430
A path is 4 centimetres on the map.

66
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,210
Find the real distance.

67
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,910
Here is Bea's working.

68
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,620
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,730
Line 2 is wrong.

70
00:03:54,780 --> 00:04:01,740
With a ratio scale, the answer is in the units you started with: centimetres, not kilometres.

71
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:04,940
120,000 centimetres is 1.2 kilometres.

72
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:08,600
That is a sensible length for a path.

73
00:04:08,650 --> 00:04:11,970
Many model railways use a scale of 1 to 87.

74
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:18,550
A real locomotive, 20 metres long, becomes a model about 23 centimetres long.

75
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:22,810
When you zoom in on a map on your phone, the scale changes.

76
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:28,270
1 centimetre on the screen might be 5 kilometres, or only 50 metres.

77
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:33,910
That is why digital maps show a small scale bar, which changes as you zoom.

78
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,310
One last question.

79
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,260
The scale is 1 to 50,000.

80
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,910
A real distance is 2.5 kilometres.

81
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:43,030
How many centimetres is that on the map?

82
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:46,930
Pause the video and work it out.

83
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:50,620
2.5 kilometres is 250,000 centimetres.

84
00:04:50,670 --> 00:04:52,280
Divide by 50,000.

85
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:55,840
It is 5 centimetres on the map.

86
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:59,950
To remember: from the map to real life, multiply by the scale.

87
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,750
From real life to the map, divide.

88
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:08,770
A ratio scale, like 1 to 50,000, uses the same unit on both sides.

89
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:15,830
100 centimetres is 1 metre, and 100,000 centimetres is 1 kilometre.

90
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:19,260
Always check that your answer is sensible.

91
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:24,670
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.1 on Camday.
